<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's CMVM okays day trade public debt on OTC.</title>
<headline>Portugal's CMVM okays day trade public debt on OTC.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) has approved a regulation that permits day trade in public debt on the Over the Counter (OTC) market, a CMVM official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The board of the CMVM has approved an alteration in regulations that authorises day trade operations in the OTC market,&quot; the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The new regulation, which will allow buying and selling of the same debt instrument in one day, will become effective on the day after its publication in the Lisbon bourse bulletin.</p>
<p>-- Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
